			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jawnsy\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jawnsy</span></a></span> And as with all Sony cameras, you need to set that “Auto Power OFF Temp” setting to high so that the camera doesn’t shut down too quickly when it gets hot. In my case the camera still died on me in the middle of a workshop, so I’m now powering it with a dummy battery instead of the USB cable and it has a heat sink and a USB-powered (and speed-controlled) Noctua fan at the back …😅 Here you can see the madness: <a href=\"https://matthiasott.com/notes/tour-de-noise\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">matthiasott.com/notes/tour-de-</span><span class=\"invisible\">noise</span></a></p>",
